ors on resume and apply `soft_fail` to the same exception types as the regular sensor execution path: `AirflowSensorTimeout`, `AirflowTaskTimeout`, and `AirflowFailException`.\n\nAlso catch `AirflowTaskTimeout` on resume so both `soft_fail` and `never_fail` can convert it to a skip. This extends `never_fail` handling for task timeouts; its handling of other errors is unchanged.\n\nValidation:\n- Updated sensor test file: 52 passed on upstream main at `9ad8d78c27` (Python 3.11, Breeze).\n- Identical tests against the original implementation at `7a479a62e6`: 5 failed, 47 passed. Failures cover generic errors, missing resources, trigger failure, and task timeouts under both flags.\n- Ruff, pre-commit checks (including Task SDK mypy), and applicable manual checks passed.\n\nThis follows the behavior discussed in the closed, unmerged PR #72053. Full worker/triggerer integration has not been tested.\n\ncloses: #71255\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes — Codex (GPT-6); Antigravity assisted with review.\n\nGenerated-by: Codex (GPT-6) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/75004/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/75004/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]]
